From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valentin rameau <valentin.rameau@outlook.fr>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 02:18:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 09/33] Runner support for the PS Vita host

Build/portability fixes so the runner cross-compiles under VitaSDK, plus
the hooks the Vita host needs to diagnose guest-side failures.

Portability:
- host_paths.c: __APPLE__ is defined when cross-compiling for Vita on a
  Mac, so the mach-o/dyld.h include and the _NSGetExecutablePath branch
  were being selected for an ARM Vita target. Gate both on !__vita__.
- sdl_compat.h: accept <SDL2/SDL.h> as well as <SDL.h>.
- vita_getenv.c: getenv() stub for a platform with no environment. The
  runner reads many SNESRECOMP_* vars for diagnostics; linked through
  -Wl,--wrap=getenv.

Diagnosis hooks. The Vita logs over UDP and has no usable stderr, so the
existing FILE*-based dumps are unreachable there:
- interp_bridge_recent_step() reads the interpreter's step ring
  programmatically.
- An optional (VITA-only) off-rails latch records the mapped -> unmapped
  control-flow crossing at the instruction where it happens. The step
  ring holds 8192 entries and a wedge in unmapped space runs far longer
  than that, so by bail time the ring contains only the wedge loop and
  the crossing itself is long gone.
- common_rtl.c WriteReg: optional (VITA-only) callback on $2100-$213F
  writes, so the host can trace the registers that decide whether a
  frame renders at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
